/F2 12 Tf (21. DOCUMENTATION-FRIENDLY SUMMARY) Tj
/F1 11 Tf
T*
() Tj
T*
(VetClinicSystem is a role-based veterinary clinic management website that supports public visitors,) Tj
T*
(clients, staff, and administrators. The system focuses on surgery request scheduling, pet) Tj
T*
(management, medical history tracking, vaccination record management, user account handling, clinic) Tj
T*
(notifications, and role-based dashboards. Clients can register, maintain their pet information,) Tj
T*
(request surgery appointments, monitor reminders and updates, and access records related to their own) Tj
T*
(pets. Staff and admins manage operational clinic tasks such as appointment approval, scheduling,) Tj
T*
(records, vaccination data, and notifications. Admins additionally manage user accounts and overall) Tj
T*
(dashboard reporting.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The appointment workflow is centered on surgery requests. Clients or guests submit a preferred) Tj
T*
(surgery date and time, a surgery category, an emergency priority option, and case notes. The clinic) Tj
T*
(then reviews and finalizes the actual schedule. Surgery requests are controlled by availability) Tj
T*
(rules such as closed Tuesdays, holiday blocks, a one-week booking window, and a daily surgery load) Tj
T*
(system. Non-emergency requests are limited to 5 surgery points per day, where minor, moderate, and) Tj
T*
(major surgeries consume 1, 2, and 3 points respectively. Emergency requests bypass that capacity) Tj
